# Programs AI Assistant

## Scope (where it is enabled)

Mount `<ProgramsAIAssistant />` only via:

- [`src/app/programs/layout.tsx`](src/app/programs/layout.tsx) — `/programs`
- [`src/app/category/layout.tsx`](src/app/category/layout.tsx) — `/category/[categorySlug]` and `/category/.../instance/[instanceId]`

Do **not** enable on admin, coach, or location/franchise pages unless explicitly requested. Site-wide `AIChatButton` remains a no-op.

## Stack

| Piece | Location |
|-------|----------|
| UI launcher + chat panel | `src/components/programs-ai/` |
| React context (open/collapse) | `src/contexts/programs-ai-assistant-context.tsx` |
| Client session | `src/lib/programs-ai-session.ts` |
| System prompt | `src/lib/programs-ai-prompt.ts` |
| API (streaming) | `POST /api/ai/programs-chat` — `@ai-sdk/deepseek` `createDeepSeek` (not `@ai-sdk/openai`; OpenAI provider sends `developer` role) |

## Environment

```env
NEXT_PUBLIC_PROGRAMS_AI_ASSISTANT_ENABLED=true   # show launcher, chat, CTA; allow API (default off if unset)
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=          # required when assistant enabled
DEEPSEEK_BASE_URL=https://api.deepseek.com   # optional override
DEEPSEEK_MODEL=deepseek-chat                   # optional override
```

Toggle flag in `.env.local` and restart `npm run dev`. Never commit keys. Do not use `DEEPSEEK_API_KEY` on the client.

Assistant replies render with `ProgramsAIChatMarkdown` (`react-markdown`); user messages stay plain text.

## Session lifecycle (client)

Stored in `localStorage` key `blaze-programs-ai-session`:

| Event | Behavior |
|-------|----------|
| **Start** | First visit or expired idle → new `sessionId` (UUID) |
| **Persist** | Same `sessionId` across `/programs` and `/category/*` navigation; `useChat({ id: sessionId })` keeps message history |
| **Activity** | `lastActivityAt` updated on each user send |
| **End (idle)** | After `PROGRAMS_AI_SESSION_IDLE_MS` (30 min) without activity → session discarded on next load |
| **End (explicit)** | User clicks **New conversation** (rotate icon in chat header) → new `sessionId`, welcome message reset |

Sessions are **not** stored server-side; only used for client chat continuity and optional API logging.

## UI states

1. **Launcher expanded** (default) — horizontal card, bottom-right, `position: fixed`, English copy, “Chat” opens panel
2. **Launcher collapsed** — circular icon only; click to re-expand
3. **Chat open** — panel above launcher; header shows **one** bot icon (no avatar row)
4. **Chat minimized** — header strip only; chevron toggles expand/minimize

Use `useProgramsAIAssistant().openChat()` from in-page CTAs (programs/category sections).

## Copy and hierarchy

- English only in assistant UI and prompts
- Use Web product terms: Campus, Location, Program (Explore/Learn/Compete), Activity, Session — see `product-hierarchy` rule
- Do not invent prices, dates, or seat counts; point users to catalog session cards / enrollment links

## Do not

- Switch programs assistant to Gemini without product approval (franchise `/api/ai/chat` may still use Gemini)
- Add unsubscribe or newsletter logic here
- Persist full transcripts server-side without a designed retention policy
- Enable physical template DELETE patterns in admin (unrelated)
